      "messageId": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To “open a workspace/repo in Git,” you usually do one of these:\n\n1. Open an existing local repo in terminal:\n   - `cd C:\\path\\to\\your\\repo`\n   - `git status`  \n   If this works, you’re already in that repo.\n\n2. Clone a remote repo, then open it:\n   - `git clone https://github.com/owner/repo.git`\n   - `cd repo`\n   - `git status`\n\n3. Turn a normal folder into a Git repo:\n   - `cd C:\\path\\to\\folder`\n   - `git init`\n   - `git status`\n\nIf you mean opening it in VS Code:\n- `code C:\\path\\to\\repo`  \n(or open VS Code, then **File → Open Folder** and pick the repo folder)."
        }
      ],
